   "detail": "3 holding(s) print a rate and a value that describe the holding's LAST DEPOSITORY MOVEMENT, not its balance — e.g. ICICI LIQF D-GROWTH: 46654.378 held, rate 394.625, value 11909782.5, which is 30180.000 units, the quantity of that movement. So these carry their units and no market value; the rate and value are kept as `lastMovementRate` / `lastMovementValue`, a transaction price rather than a valuation. The value column sums to the printed Total Holding Valuation of Rs 75769571.51 to the rupee, so every row was read — and that total is a sum of last-movement values, not what the account is worth."
